# globals.css custom classes

Applies when editing [`frontend/app/globals.css`](../../frontend/app/globals.css).

## Before adding or renaming

Stop and **AskQuestion** before you:

- Add a new `@utility …`
- Add a bespoke single-purpose class meant for repeated use in JSX
- Duplicate styling that Tailwind utilities or `cn()` on molecules/organisms can express

Briefly state: what you searched, existing `@utility` / tokens considered, and why composition is insufficient.

## Prefer (in order)

1. **Tailwind + `cn()`** on shared components (`components/molecules/`, `components/organisms/`)
2. **Existing `@utility`** — e.g. `shadow-zone-card`, `max-w-form`, `bg-login-page`, `bg-page-wash`, layout utilities (`px-page`, `max-w-crud-page`)
3. **CSS variables** in `:root` / `.dark` and shadcn `@theme inline` bridge — token layer per [design-system.mdc](design-system.mdc); no extra approval for semantic variables when design tokens change

## Do not

- Add a new `@utility` for one page or one screen without user approval
- Copy the same gradient/shadow block under a second name — reuse or bundle on a molecule instead
